      "overall_structure": {
        "value": "After annealing at 550 °C for 5 h the 3Cr strip is still composed of an austenite (γ) matrix plus δ-ferrite; κ-carbide precipitation remains suppressed (SADP superlattice very weak/absent), the δ-ferrite contains DO3 ordered domains, and the austenite dislocation density is reduced relative to the as-cast 3Cr strip but still higher than the annealed 0Cr strip. SEM shows a smooth grey matrix with dispersed dark second-phase particles and no resolvable grain boundary/dendritic network."
